{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1096810-wanting-to-make-a-character-creation-program","id":1096810,"title":"Wanting to make a character creation program","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T11:55:35-07:00","id":1096810,"title":"Wanting to make a character creation program","content":"Back when I was getting into tabletop RPGs, a friend introduced me to a character creator for Vampire: The Masquerade. It was an old program, and only worked some of the time, but the ease of having that kind of resource meant that making a character was far easier for me to do for an unfamiliar system. It tallied points put into various fields (Mental, Physical and Social), how much higher or lower you were to the limit of those fields, and it also took into account Merits and Flaws in terms of the points available. It had many merits and flaws to select from, as well as different natures and dispositions, and even if it didn't have anything like that, it still let you enter in the names and values yourself.<br /> <br /> I'm looking to make a program like that for modern Chronicles of Darkness games. Only problem (well, one of the problems) is that I don't know how to code, and thus don't know what kind of coding to focus on. There are many online resources to look into, though I imagine that it still won't be a quick thing for me to put together; I just need a direction to look into. This would just be a fan project, in no way monetized, and it has ever chance at not being finished.<br /> <br /> I still would like to give it a try. Thanks for reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jp